{
  "id": "Compound::DB00898 - Gene::1559",
  "verbalization": "Ethanol is implicated in the interaction with Cyp2c9 through a series of molecular pathways involving Cyp2c19. The evidence suggests that ethanol binds to Cyp2c19, which then participates in the oxidation of limonene, a process catalyzed by the enzyme (r)-limonene 6-monooxygenase or (s)-limonene 7-monooxygenase. These activities are ultimately linked to Cyp2c9, indicating a potential role for Cyp2c9 in the metabolic activation of limonene derivatives. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust connection, though the specific isoform of limonene being oxidized may vary, contributing to the distinct pathways observed. The integration of these mechanisms highlights a possible dependency on Cyp2c9 in the metabolic processing of limonene, though the exact functional role remains to be elucidated.",
